{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"ADR LANDED, BUT THIS TICKET IS NOT CLOSEABLE YET — one acceptance criterion is genuinely unmet and I am not ticking it.\n\nMERGED: Gerrit 1339 reached LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 and merged as d416ab9846 \"8625: ADR 0059 for the LLM provider seam\". Diff: docs/adr/0059-llm-provider-seam-and-support-tiers.md (+992, new) and docs/llm-framework.md (+132/-19). ADR 0059 is present on main (confirmed by listing docs/adr/). docs/env-vars.md was deliberately NOT modified: it is generated, and gen_env_registry.py --check exits 0 both before and after because this change adds no new env-var READ in Python.\n\nWHAT REMAINS, and it is real work rather than bookkeeping:\n* AC2 [operator-attested] requires that EVERY RUNNABLE COMMAND in docs/llm-framework.md's provider section has been EXECUTED and produced the documented output. That has not been done. It is not satisfiable by inspection, and the ADR landing does not discharge it. Whoever picks this up must actually run those commands and record the outputs on this ticket. Note the section was edited by this very change, so the command set is the POST-change one.\n* AC1 (ADR exists, is Accepted, names each rejected alternative) and AC3 (docs state per-tier guarantees and what a consumer may infer) are almost certainly satisfied by the landed ADR, but I did not verify them line by line against the merged text and so did not tick them. Verify against d416ab9846 rather than against the pre-merge draft.\n* AC4 [operator-attested] (the generator produces NO diff to docs/env-vars.md) has its evidence above and can be ticked once someone confirms the exit code themselves.\n\nCORRECTIONS THE LANDED ADR CARRIES, recorded here so they are findable from this ticket: nine rotted file:line anchors were fixed, and EIGHT config.py:NNN anchors were disambiguated because they resolve correctly only against src/rebar/llm/config.py and land on unrelated text against the top-level src/rebar/config.py. The draft's botocore version was corrected from 1.43.58 to the 1.43.62 the code now records. The epic's false \"--extra bedrock or the gate dies\" premise is recorded as correction #1 with the reasoning error named: absence of the EXTRA was taken to imply absence of the MODULE, and confirmed by READING packaging rather than EXECUTING the import."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785818006280473001,"uuid":"04b471c2-ce4f-4821-9550-457ec6cbb1d3"}